      "card_ids": ["C20", "C23", "C43", "C48", "C55"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct measured absolute oral bioavailability for the exact query molecule.",
    "No human pharmacokinetic data for the specific cyclobutyl guanine nucleoside scaffold.",
    "Uncertainty regarding transporter-mediated absorption and metabolic stability, such as potential deamination of the guanine base.",
    "Formulation and dose for the query are not specified beyond the fasted condition.",
    "Species differences in nucleoside analog F values, e.g., zalcitabine 80% in humans versus 30% in mice, limit quantitative extrapolation."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 adds further nucleoside analog absolute F values (zalcitabine 30% in mice; ddA/ddI 30–93% across species; ddI 30–54%) that all remain ≥20%, reinforcing the prior high prediction. Non-nucleoside low-bioavailability records are not transferable to this guanine carbocyclic nucleoside. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

